":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 1: 'Add \"archived\": \"Done\" to config.local_to_jira_status and its parity twin ... LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA.' — only archived is added","AC1: 'a bound deleted ticket whose Jira issue is To Do yields one outbound update {status: \"Done\"}'","Step 1: 'SKIP or an absent key yields no target.' — an absent 'deleted' key would produce no target"],"finding":"The plan adds only 'archived' to the status maps but AC1 requires a bound DELETED ticket to emit {status: Done} by default; the plan never states that 'deleted' is already present in config.local_to_jira_status / value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA, so if it is absent the resolver returns no target and classify yields RETIRE_TERMINAL with no mutation, contradicting AC1.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffe05ce282f987626","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 + AC line 1","norm_id":"n0d44627adfb14be4","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["No [mapping] block; bound deleted ticket; Jira issue To Do — resolver keyed by 'deleted' returns absent → RETIRE_TERMINAL instead of {status: Done}"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Confirm the current contents of the base map and, if 'deleted' is absent, add 'deleted': 'Done' alongside 'archived': 'Done' in both config.local_to_jira_status and LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify exactly how the binding walk derives the Jira project key for effective_status_map (resolve from the binding/ticket vs. parse the bound Jira key prefix) and confirm it works when the local ticket is deleted/unreadable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.468,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'config.effective_status_map(<project key of the bound Jira key>, root=repo_root)'","outbound_effective_maps.py:40 resolves project_key via projects_store.resolve_project(ticket, mapping), not by parsing the Jira key","fetcher.py:337 derives a project key as first_key.rsplit('-', 1)[0]","A deleted local ticket's record may be unreadable by local_reader, making ticket-based resolution unavailable"],"finding":"The plan under-specifies how the binding walk derives the Jira project key used to key effective_status_map for an off-snapshot (possibly deleted) local ticket. The existing outbound path (outbound_effective_maps.py) resolves the key via projects_store.resolve_project(ticket, mapping), but a DELETED local ticket may be unreadable, so that route may be unavailable; the alternative is parsing the Jira key prefix (fetcher.py uses first_key.rsplit('-',1)[0]). The archived='Cancelled' override acceptance criterion depends on this derivation being correct.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd213d4ca72fba393","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1; AC 'a project override archived = \"Cancelled\" yields {status: \"Cancelled\"}'","norm_id":"nf0771361218f3590","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A deleted local ticket bound to DIG-123 where [mapping.projects.DIG.status_map] sets archived/deleted = Cancelled","The project-override AC cannot pass if the walk cannot recover the project key for a deleted ticket"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the project key is derived from the bound Jira key's prefix (e.g. DIG-123 -> DIG, mirroring fetcher.py's rsplit) since a deleted ticket's record may be unavailable, and note which helper is the single source of that grammar.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Acknowledge and test the breaker double-gating of a terminal cohort (transition pass then retire pass) and state the intended operator workflow when a cohort exceeds max_acting_fraction at both steps.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan step 2: 'RETIRE_TERMINAL joins ACTING_KINDS, so mass retirement stays under the existing max_acting_fraction breaker'","Plan step 3: 'a pass that closes the issue leaves the binding, and the next pass that observes the target ... status retires it'","classify.py:65 ACTING_KINDS and check_blast_radius count every acting decision uniformly","AC #7 tests only that 14 retirements are refused — not that the SAME cohort is gated at both the transition and the retire step"],"finding":"The plan routes a terminal cohort through the breaker twice without acknowledging it: TERMINAL_TRANSITION (pass N) and RETIRE_TERMINAL (pass N+1, after the close is observed) are both in ACTING_KINDS, so the same cohort that required lifting max_acting_fraction to transition will re-hit the identical breaker as RETIRE_TERMINAL on the confirming pass. The ADP motivation (19/130 held by the breaker) means an operator who raises the cap to let the transitions fire must then observe the same cohort refused again at the retire step until the cap is raised a second time.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8dbb9eab843e67f9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 2-3; AC #7 (breaker)","norm_id":"n35e2f5f52d912709","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ADP: 19 deleted stories blocked at 19/130 > 0.1; operator raises the cap, 19 transitions fire; next pass 19 RETIRE_TERMINAL decisions are refused by the unchanged cap, leaving 19 live bindings re-closing nothing but perpetually gated"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance criterion that a cohort which transitioned under a raised cap is then retired (not permanently refused) on the confirming pass, and document that mass terminal cohorts cross the breaker twice.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_a